dsv41 patch 0048 (20.10.2026): mHC sublayer boundary in one launch with TileLang's bits (vllm_exl3_moe plugin only).
At every overlapped mHC boundary (patch 0014's side stream, <= 16 rows in FULL graphs) the main stream runs two
one-block-per-token TileLang kernels: mhc_post_tilelang (16.4 us mean at 6 rows on GB10) and
mhc_pre_big_fuse_with_norm in split mode "input" (15.4 us), 66 of the 80 boundaries a round, both on the critical path
(profile of 19.10.2026, 1 stream: 2.1 ms of a 38.9 ms round). Patch 0021's chunked kernel already fuses them, but adds the
RMSNorm's sum of squares in another order (rounding class) and normalizes in a serial last-block tail.
post_collapse_exact: one block a token, 128 threads, every load of the token in flight at once; thread (q, h) owns
the columns b * 1024 + h * 512 + q * 8 + [0, 8) of each 1024-column block, which is TileLang thread q's slot half h in
the generated "input" kernel (64 collapse threads, hidden_block 1024). So every rounding is TileLang's: the post as
v = c * d; v = v + a * b (same C form, so nvcc contracts the same FMAs), bf16 rounding, the collapse from the rounded
streams in stream order, the per-slot fma chain of squares over the blocks, the slot order 0, 8, 1, 9, ..., 7, 15,
the 64-thread butterfly (q ^ 32 first, as tl::AllReduce), rsqrtf(sum / H + eps) with IEEE division (neither side is
built with fast math), and (v * rsqrt) * w. The post's outputs stay in registers for the collapse and the RMSNorm.
Bit-equal to the two TileLang kernels by test (GPU test against the real TileLang kernels: residual_out and layer_input
as int16 views, 1..16 and 24 rows, special values, graph replay); -DMHCX_TREE=1 (EXL3_MHC_FLAGS) builds the other butterfly
order should the installed tl::AllReduce differ. vLLM side unchanged: patch 0021's hook in ops/mhc.py calls
vllm_exl3_moe.mhc.post_collapse, which now dispatches by mode.
Switch: VLLM_DSV41_MHC_FUSED_POST = 0 (default: the TileLang pair, unchanged), 1 (0021's kernel), 2 (this kernel).
Read at import; needs a serve restart. H 5120 (V4.1-Flash) or 7168; other sizes keep the TileLang pair.
Measured (20.10.2026, GB10, 2000 MHz): bit test passed; one boundary in the decode graph 6.4 -> 3.6 us; T = 0 texts
identical to the TileLang pair (8/8); serve, VLLM_DSV41_MHC_FUSED_POST=2 against 0: geometric mean over all T = 1
cells +0.99 %. We run it with 2.

